        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Russia pummels Ukraine, hitting regions far from the front lines Europe Issued on: 14/05/2026 - 12:52 Russia is intensifying its daytime attacks on Ukraine, including on regions sometimes far from the front lines. On Wednesday, Moscow launched at least 800 drones against Ukraine, according to Volodymyr Zelensky. The attacks continued into Thursday morning, killing at least six people and wounding dozens of others. Story by Simon Moritz and Camille Corcoran. 800 drones in 24 hours? Russia launches massive daytime barrage on Ukraine 14/05/2026 Europe A massive overnight barrage on Kyiv splits a residential building in two 14/05/2026 Europe European Union adopts new sanctions Israeli settlers over violence in West Bank 12/05/2026 Europe Europe weighs Putin’s ceasefire signals and security proposals 10/05/2026 Europe Russia, Ukraine trade blame over ceasefire violations 10/05/2026 Europe Passengers disembark from Hantavirus-hit cruise ship in Canary Islands 10/05/2026 Europe 'Nothing like COVID': Expert urges calm over hantavirus outbreak on cruise ship 10/05/2026 Europe Scottish independence calls grow after Labour losses shake Starmer’s leadership 10/05/2026 Europe Hantavirus poses 'very little risk' to wider public, health expert says 10/05/2026 Europe"
